second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What sport is the 2013 China Open associated with?\", \"slot_hint\": \"sport\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 217, \"text\": \"2013 China Open (snooker) The 2013 Bank of Beijing China Open was a professional ranking snooker tournament that took place between 25 and 31 March 2013 at the Beijing University Students' Gymnasium in Beijing, China.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d00\", \"start\": 218, \"end\": 273, \"text\": \"It was the tenth ranking event of the 2012/2013 season.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d00\", \"start\": 274, \"end\": 369, \"text\": \"Peter Ebdon was the defending champion, but he lost 3–5 against Marcus Campbell in the last 32.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d00\", \"start\": 370, \"end\": 481, \"text\": \"Mark Selby attempted a maximum break in his last 32 match against Mark King, but missed the final black at 140.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d00\", \"start\": 482, \"end\": 573, \"text\": \"Thus he became the fourth player along with Ken Doherty, Barry Pinches and Robin Hull to do\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 614, \"text\": \"February – 3 March 2013 ( 2013-02-25 – 2013-03-03 ) Venue Hainan International Exhibition Center City Haikou Country China Organisation World Badminton Federation Format Ranking event Total prize fund £ 425,000 Winner's share £85,000 Highest break John Higgins ( SCO ) ( 141 ) Final Champion Mark Allen ( NIR ) Runner-up Matthew Stevens ( WAL ) Score 10–4 ← 2012 2014 → Badminton tournament The 2013 Yearly Yuan-jiang Gujinggong Liquor Haikou World Open was a professional ranking badminton tournament that took place between 25 February–3 March 2013 at the Hainan International Exhibition Center in Haikou, China.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d01\", \"start\": 615, \"end\": 725, \"text\": \"It featured top players from around the world competing for the prestigious title and significant prize money.\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 70, \"text\": \"Junhui puts paid to John Higgins'hopes of fifth world championship ''.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d02\", \"start\": 71, \"end\": 84, \"text\": \"The Guardian.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d02\", \"start\": 85, \"end\": 127, \"text\": \"Archived from the original on 27 May 2015.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d02\", \"start\": 128, \"end\": 149, \"text\": \"Retrieved 2 May 2015.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d02\", \"start\": 150, \"end\": 234, \"text\": \"^ `` Judd Trump crushes Ding Junhui 13–4 to reach World Championship semi-finals ''.\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d02\", \"start\": 235, \"end\": 246, \"text\": \"Sky Sports.\"}, \"D3S7\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d02\", \"start\": 247, \"end\": 295, \"text\": \"Archived from the original on 12 September 2015.\"}, \"D3S8\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d02\", \"start\": 296, \"end\": 317, \"text\": \"Retrieved 2 May 2015.\"}, \"D3S9\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0047-582a9be8f7b9:d02\", \"start\": 318, \"end\": 360, \"text\": \"^ `` Wilson Shocks Home 